<h1>George A. Cardenas</h1>
<p>Board of Review, 1st District, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: Democratic. Incumbent.</p>
<p><a href="https://georgecardenas.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (georgecardenas.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Cardenas says his focus is fairness for every property owner through fair appeals, transparent policy, and direct constituent services. His listed initiatives include a property tax transparency dashboard with township-level and class-level trends, advocacy for circuit breaker relief for income-constrained homeowners, appeal-readiness workshops so residents file complete appeals on time, a single process map linking the Assessor, Board of Review, Treasurer, and Clerk, and a planned small business and commercial equity review.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Cardenas served 20 years as Chicago&#39;s 12th Ward alderman, is a U.S. Navy veteran, and worked for Fortune 500 companies before entering government.</p>
